  "PublishCopy": {
    "title": "Nobody knows exactly why keyboards are QWERTY",
    "description": "Your keyboard's layout is over 150 years old, and nobody's completely sure why it's in this order.\nNewspaper editor Christopher Latham Sholes designed it in the early 1870s, and his typewriter was sold to Remington in 1873. The typebar-jamming story, the telegraph-operator theory and the 'TYPEWRITER on the top row' tale are all still debated.",
